From 6ab2ac182e91c90bea2e09db014e7676a8252ef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:39:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: mtk_ccci: Add CCCI RPC responder for MT6789

Add Gen95 CCCI kernel RPC responder (ch=32 -> ch=33 over CCIF0 Q1) to
unblock modem HS2 completion on MT6789 (Advan X1):

- Add mtk_ccci_tx_send() with per-channel 15-bit sequence counter and
  Gen95 assert_bit semantics (assert_bit=1 during HS1->HS2 single-task
  phase, 0 once READY) plus serialized CCIF0 ringbuffer write + doorbell.
- Move CCIF0 RX draining onto a dedicated ordered unbound workqueue
  (mtk_ccci_rx) with a pre-allocated 4 KiB RX buffer so RX/RPC replies
  cannot deadlock against mtk_ccci_boot_work() waiting on hs2_comp.
- Implement mtk_ccci_rpc_handle() in mtk_ccci_rpc.c with strictly
  Advan X1-sourced SIM hot-plug EINT, GPIO mapping, AUXADC, and md_attr
  values (from runtime_merged.dts, ccci_md_all.ko, and ccci_dump.log).
- Keep ch=14 (CCCI_CH_FS_RX) strictly log-only (never touching NVRAM)
  and hex-dump opcode + first 64 bytes of any unhandled RPC or non-RPC
  packet.
- Expose read-only rpc_count sysfs telemetry attribute.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
